<article class="env-lemma" id="0CWB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CWB">Lemma <span data-tag="0CWB">77.8.4</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0CWA" data-tag="0CWA">77.8.1</a>. Let $T \subset S$ be a subset. Let $s \in S$ be in the closure of $T$. For $t \in T$, let $u_ t$ be the pullback of $u$ to $X_ t$ and let $u_ s$ be the pullback of $u$ to $X_ s$. If $X$ is locally of finite presentation over $S$, $\mathcal{G}$ is of finite presentation<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001481286" id="a0001481286-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>, and $u_ t = 0$ for all $t \in T$, then $u_ s = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To check whether $u_ s$ is zero, is étale local on the fibre $X_ s$. Hence we may pick a point $x \in |X_ s| \subset |X|$ and check in an étale neighbourhood. Choose 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (X, x) \ar[d] &  (X', x') \ar[l]^ g \ar[d] \\  (S, s) &  (S', s') \ar[l] }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as in Proposition <a href="/tag/0CVY" data-tag="0CVY">77.5.1</a>. Let $T' \subset S'$ be the inverse image of $T$. Observe that $s'$ is in the closure of $T'$ because $S' \to S$ is open. Hence we reduce to the algebra problem described in the next paragraph. 
    <p>
      We have an $R$-module map $u : M \to N$ such that $N$ is projective as an $R$-module and such that $u_ t : M \otimes _ R \kappa (t) \to N \otimes _ R \kappa (t)$ is zero for each $t \in T$. Problem: show that $u_ s = 0$. Let $I \subset R$ be the ideal defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/083L" data-tag="083L">77.8.3</a>. Then $I$ maps to zero in $\kappa (t)$ for all $t \in T$. Hence $T \subset V(I)$. Since $s$ is in the closure of $T$ we see that $s \in V(I)$. Hence $u_ s = 0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>